# E0200: a use-after-free the compiler used to accept. `sv` views `s`'s
# buffer; moving `s` out and growing the new owner reallocates, and `sv` reads
# freed memory. Verified under ASan before this rule existed.
main: function is {
    s: "abcdefghij".string
    sv: s.stringView
    g: s.take
    g.append s: "0123456789012345678901234567890123456789".string
    print "sv=\{sv}"
    print "g=\{g}"
}
